 ## Overview
-Line Integral Convolution (LIC) is a texture-based flow visualization method that maps a scalar noise field onto a vector field by integrating the noise along streamlines, producing a streak-like texture that reveals global flow direction [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial][S3]. It differs from streamline-based methods by densely displaying direction information across the entire field without requiring user-defined seed points, though it does not inherently encode flow direction (positive/negative) or speed magnitude [S3].
