 ## How it works
 **Inputs and Outputs:**
-*   **Input 1:** A vector field $\mathbf{V}(x,y)$ defined on a 2D grid [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Input 2:** A scalar noise texture $F_{in}$ (typically white noise) with the same resolution as the vector field [S2, unofficial].
-*   **Output:** A scalar field $F_{out}$ representing the convolved texture [S1, unofficial].
