 ### [Image Space Fabric Visualization](10569-image-space-fabric-visualization.md)
-Projects tensor data into image space and advects noise along eigenvectors on GPU FBOs for real-time fabric-like visualization of symmetric tensor fields. Choose for interactive symmetric tensor field exploration on modern GPUs.
+Projects tensor data into image space and advects noise along eigenvectors on GPU FBOs for real-time fabric-like visualization of symmetric tensor fields.
 
 ### [Box Filter Dye Advection](12157-box-filter-dye-advection.md)
-Replaces the Hanning filter with a box filter and introduces phase-shifting to animate dye advection along streamlines over time. Choose when temporal flow animation is required without spatial length variation.
+Replaces the Hanning filter with a box filter and introduces phase-shifting to animate dye advection along streamlines over time.
 
 ### [Variable Convolution Length for Dye](12158-variable-convolution-length-for-dye.md)
-Decouples the convolution length of the dye from the global LIC texture, allowing long dye trails without degrading the underlying LIC texture's contrast or efficiency. Choose when highlighting long-range flow features is critical without sacrificing local texture quality.
+Decouples the convolution length of the dye from the global LIC texture, allowing long dye trails without degrading the underlying LIC texture's contrast or efficiency.
 
 ### [Variable Step Euler LIC](12778-variable-step-euler-lic.md)
-Uses variable step Euler's method to compute curved field lines for each pixel, capturing small-scale structures like eddies better than straight-line approximations. Choose when high-fidelity capture of local curvature and vortices is required.
+Uses variable step Euler's method to compute curved field lines for each pixel, capturing small-scale structures like eddies better than straight-line approximations.
 
 ### Aliasing Reduction via Trilinear Interpolation
-Uses trilinear interpolation during rendering to reduce the 'stair-stepped' aliasing appearance of voxel-based field lines in LIC textures. This technique smooths field lines and creates a halo effect for better separation of lines, which is particularly important for sparse textures like those in Seed LIC [S4, unofficial].
